ose the restaurant.\n\nThe strongest point I could add is what your 3% increases come to: $5,100 rises to about $5,740 by year five, which is more than he's asking. He gets more by the end of the lease if he keeps you.\n\nFill in your restaurant's name in the subject line before you send it.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Lease renewal for [Restaurant Name]\n\nDear Frank,\n\nThank you for sending the renewal terms. I'd like to stay in the space, and I hope we can agree on a number that works for both of us.\n\nI can't pay $5,650 a month. At that rent, I couldn't keep the restaurant open. What I can offer is $5,100 a month on a new five-year lease, with 3% increases each year after the first. That would bring the rent to about $5,740 by the fifth year, which is more than your proposed figure, and you'd have a tenant you already know.\n\nA few things I hope you'll consider:\n\n- I've been in this space for ten years, over two leases.\n- In 2019 I put about $70,000 into the kitchen, including a new hood system that stays with the building.\n- The unit two doors down has been listed at $28 a square foot for 14 months. Your proposal works out to about $29 a foot for my space.\n\nI understand a coffee chain has asked about the space. I'd only ask you to compare that with steady rent from a tenant who is already here and has already invested in the building.\n\nCould you let me know your answer by June 1? That would give me time to plan before the lease ends in August. I'm glad to meet in person if that's easier.\n\nThank you, Frank. I appreciate the last ten years, and I hope we can keep going.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your name]\n[Restaurant Name]\n[Phone]\n</final_document>","ttft_ms":12040,"type":"result","duration_ms":18084,"uuid":"f53af20d-43da-4ec8-83d1-1990bbb483a2","ttft_stream_ms":656,"time_to_request_ms":136,"first_content_frame_ms":656,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":1640,"cacheR